pt09 adversarial lane, surface: intake normalization x gate morphology.
Greens the RED frozen in the previous commit.

`localDomainRelevance` was the only stage in the pipeline reading raw passage
bytes. Retrieval, clause splitting, stance, and `namesCanonSurface` — five
lines above, inside this same function — all read `normalizeText` output. The
asymmetry hid because the frame patterns are written lower-case with `/i`, so
case never exposed it; what it cost was every multi-word pattern spanning a
space. One U+00A0, the character an HTML paste yields from `&nbsp;`, turned
"a provider" into a string `provisioning-role` cannot see and the passage was
set aside `no-human-relational-frame`.

Same class, now also closed: U+202F, U+3000 and every other Unicode space
separator; a curly apostrophe where a pattern spells a straight one; an en or
em dash where a pattern spells a hyphen; a combining accent where a pattern
spells the bare letter.

Floors: domainRecall 1.0000, ignorePrecision 1.0000, junkRecall 0.8529 over
191 cases — identical before and after, and every one of the 191 verdicts and
reason codes is byte-identical. Corpus stance census: 0 of 1,298 matches move.
Neither instrument holds a non-ASCII space, which is the finding as much as
the fix is: the class is invisible to both, and reachable from the Lab's
primary intake path, since `decodeEntities` turns `&nbsp;` into U+00A0 and
nothing downstream of intake removed it.

All 18 suite steps green. No floor moved and none needed to.

